(BAS-35 - a nested construct owns its own trailing period.
 Also covers: BAS-36 (the enclosing While does not steal it), BAS-37
 (after the inner If ends, the outer sentence continues with two more
 comma-separated actions). If the While had taken the inner If's period,
 `print "tick ..."` and `increment tick` would be top-level and the loop
 would never terminate.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-35.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   tick 0
   marked
   tick 1
   tick 2
   end
)
a number called tick is 0.
While tick is less than 3,
    if tick is equal to 1 then,
        print "marked".
    print "tick {tick}",
    increment tick.
Print "end".
